{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CrossProduct","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_params_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_params_injective","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L98-L112","doc":"The `q` parameters `t_k`, `k < q`, are distinct: the inflections come `q` at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.cos_q_mul_inflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.cos_q_mul_inflection","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L89-L96","doc":"At `t_k = (2k + 1)π/q` one has `cos(q t_k) = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_radius_three_five_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_radius_three_five_seven","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The three component types of the canonical closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.inflection_iff","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L60-L81","doc":"**The inflection radius.** For `0 < q`, `r < 1` and `c² + s² = 1`, the curvature of the\ntorus embedding vanishes at `t = π/q` iff `r = 4 / (q² + 4)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:frenet-framing-is-not-an-invariant","label":"rem:frenet-framing-is-not-an-invariant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frenet-framing-is-not-an-invariant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.cross_vel_acc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.cross_vel_acc","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L52-L58","doc":"The cross product at `t = π/q` factors through `q² r - 4(1 - r)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.acc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.acc","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L48-L50","doc":"`γ''(π/q)`: `((q² r - 4(1-r)) c, (q² r - 4(1-r)) s, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.vel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusInflection.vel","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusInflection.lean#L45-L46","doc":"`γ'(π/q)` written with `c = cos(2π/q)`, `s = sin(2π/q)`: `(-2(1-r) s, 2(1-r) c, -q r)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}